course: dictionary
lesson: 12172
title: Hidden and secret
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Concealment is a noun, and it comes from the verb conceal, which means to hide something. If you know conceal, you have a clue to the meaning of concealment.
explain: It has two main meanings. The first is the act of hiding something or keeping it secret: «The concealment of the stolen jewels took the thief weeks.» The second is a hiding place or cover: «The soldiers stayed in concealment until nightfall.»
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. In a detective story, the clues show that someone is keeping the truth hidden, so concealment means hiding. Then swap in a simple word like hiding or cover and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Concealment is a noun, and it comes from the verb conceal, meaning to hide.
fact: «Concealment» can mean the act of hiding something or keeping it secret.
fact: «Concealment» can also mean a hiding place or cover, as in «in concealment».
fact: In science, animals use camouflage for concealment from their enemies.
fact: In formal and legal language, concealment of facts means hiding things you should tell.
exercise: «The detective found the concealment of the stolen jewels under the floorboards.» What does concealment mean here? | Selling something in a shop | Making a loud noise | *Hiding something or keeping it secret | Showing something to everyone
exercise: «The soldiers stayed in concealment behind the hedge.» What does concealment mean here? | *A hiding place or cover | A lot of money | A long march | A loud song
exercise: A stick insect uses its shape for concealment from hungry birds. What is the concealment for? | Showing off to the birds | *Hiding from the birds | Keeping warm in the sun | Finding food
test: «The lawyer warned that concealment of facts from the court is a serious crime.» What does concealment of facts mean? | Writing facts down | Finding new facts | Telling everyone the facts | *Hiding facts you should tell
test: «The treasure was kept in a place of concealment under the old church.» What is a place of concealment? | A school hall | *A hidden place where things are kept out of sight | An open field | A busy shop window
exam: «The fox found perfect concealment in the tall grass.» What does concealment mean in this sentence? | Very loud noise | Very hungry | Bright light | *A hiding place or cover
